# -------------------------------------------------
# SASS installation steps (Windows - Node 20.18.0)
# -------------------------------------------------
# Note: Course specifies v3.7.4, but that version doesn't exist for 'sass' package.
# Using latest stable 'sass' (Dart Sass) which is fully compatible and recommended.
# Old 'node-sass' had v3.x, but it's deprecated.

# 1. Download and install Node.js v20.18.0 (or v20.16.0 if preferred)
#    URL: https://nodejs.org/dist/v20.18.0/node-v20.18.0-x64.msi
#    Run the .msi installer (default settings)

# 2. Restart terminal / VS Code

# 3. Verify Node
node --version    # Expected: v20.18.0 (or v20.16.0)
npm --version     # Expected: 10.8.x

# 4. Install SASS globally (latest stable)
npm install -g sass

# 5. Verify SASS
sass --version    # Expected: 1.93.3 (or latest stable)